little weight"], "rationale": "The open R+7 seat and Joe Strada's massive fundraising edge keep Republicans firmly in control of this race; the lone tied poll is dated and partisan-sponsored, while ten raters and prediction markets align behind the GOP.", "watch": "A strong national Democratic midterm wave, or the July tie poll proving prescient, could pull the race back toward competitive.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 63 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Daniel Webster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 11th District sits in Republican-leaning territory northwest of Orlando, and Daniel Webster's retirement leaves an open seat that still leans the GOP's way. Joe Strada won a recount in the Republican primary over Carey Baker and enters the fall with a commanding financial position: more than $5.2 million raised, $2.2 million on hand, and some outside support. Democrat James Pericola has raised roughly $120,000, and a Libertarian is also on the ballot.\n\nRatings from ten outlets split between Likely R and Solid R, and prediction markets give Republicans about an 88% chance. The only public poll, a July survey from a Democratic-leaning firm, showed a 42-42 tie, but it predates the primary and carries little weight. The national midterm environment could tighten the race, but money, partisanship, and the ratings consensus all point to a Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -7.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1312, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1199, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0989, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1239, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1092, "margin": -8.5}]}